MAN - show manual pages››Syntax:› MAN [name] [/P|?]››Shows the help file name.MAN, .HLP,›.DOC or .TXT found in the directories›of $MANPATH (default CAR:). Files›packed with ARC are unpacked on the›fly (using $TEMP). If several match,›MAN asks which one. MAN alone lists›all pages.››Options:› /?  only tell whether the page exists› /P  do not use $PAGER››Without $PAGER the text is shown like›TYPE, without stopping. $PAGER names a›viewer to use instead; in it % marks›where the file name goes and ; stands›for a space.››Examples:› MAN DIR› MAN COPY | LESS› SET MANPATH=CAR:;D1:>DOC› SET PAGER=LESS;/C;%››See also: LESS, MORE, TYPE, FMT›